A||N||2||coachreed||Will an '88 4 cylinder work in an '86?||||1||
Z||000000||coachreed||09-29-2000||12:36 AM||||I am helping a friend with putting a new engine in his '86 SE because of a rod through the block.  I have been emailed by someone who said they have an engine but it came from an '88.  He said that the engine is set up with Distrubutorless Ignition System (DIS).  He said that I should ask people who know these cars if it can be used for this particular application.  Is there a place for a distributor on the engine with DIS, or do I need a different engine all together?  If it can't be used, is it possible to upgrade to a DIS?  What would be required?  Computer?  Wire harness?  A hole in my head?  Wait, scratch that last one.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.<P>Thanks in advance.<P>------------------<BR>Coach... I mean Randy (I often forget who I really am)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo/images/coachbanner.jpg"> </A><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-29-2000||02:38 AM||||No. it won't work. not easily any way. read my cave article about the 4 cyls. link at bottom of page.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||09-29-2000||02:40 AM||||as far as I know, to put a DIS/87-88 Duke in a non-DIS car you will need the ECM & Harness from the DIS car. I think the mounts are the same form 86 up on 4-cyls. so I think that it will bolt in.||||reg||1
